<dc:title>James McGirk</dc:title>
<dc:description>James McGirk was the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/158&quot;&gt;first person to be executed&lt;/a&gt; in the District of Columbia on October 28, 1802. He was found guilty of murdering his wife. At this time, the gallows were located on the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/59&quot;&gt;Capitol&lt;/a&gt; Grounds, between where the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/21&quot;&gt;Grant&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/13&quot;&gt;Garfield&lt;/a&gt; statues stand today.</dc:description>
